{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01JKT2mCM2ZQ7Bw1uTpnJ7XH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N8vRWcVUN9BX31g3YyL55z","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 6=Strong Accept). Your focus areas are **Methods** and **Experiments**.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\n**Title**: ContamCal: Calibrating Benchmark Scores for Training Data Contamination via Contamination-Augmented Item Response Theory\n\n**Core idea**: A two-stage framework bridging contamination detection and score calibration. Stage 1 computes item-level contamination exposure via 4 detection signals (embedding similarity, Min-K++, ConStat, LLM self-critique) aggregated through RRF. Stage 2 fits a contamination-augmented 4PL IRT model with per-benchmark γ_k and a measurement error model that propagates signal uncertainty into Bayesian posteriors.\n\n**Key results**: 1.8pp MAE (bootstrap 95% CI [1.2, 2.4]) with 94% credible interval coverage on controlled contamination injection across Qwen2.5 (0.5B-7B) and Llama-3.2-1B, 3 benchmarks (MMLU, GSM8K, ARC-C), 5 dosages, 3 seeds. 7 baselines compared.\n\n## Paper Content (13 pages)\n\n### Method (Section 3)\n- **Stage 1**: 4 signals computed per item: S1 Embedding Similarity (cosine sim to nearest training neighbor, training-data-independent), S2 Min-K++ (token-level probability outlier, needs logits), S3 ConStat (original vs paraphrase performance gap), S4 Self-Critique (LLM self-assessment of familiarity). Aggregated via RRF: RRF(i) = Σ 1/(k + r_s(i)), k=60, normalized to [0,1] for continuous exposure τ̂_i.\n- **Stage 2**: 4PL+γ IRT: P(Y_ij=1 | θ_j, ξ_i, τ_i) = c_i + (d_i - c_i)/(1 + exp(-a_i(θ_j + γ_k·τ_i - b_i))). θ_j = model ability, a_i = discrimination, b_i = difficulty, c_i = guessing, d_i = upper asymptote, τ_i = latent exposure, γ_k = per-benchmark contamination susceptibility.\n- Calibrated score: s^calib = (1/n_k) Σ P(Y_ij=1 | θ_j, ξ_i, τ_i=0)\n- **Measurement Error Model**: τ̂_i = τ_i + ε_i, ε_i ~ N(0, σ_e²), σ_e estimated from FP/FN rates.\n- **Per-benchmark γ_k**: Captures heterogeneity (GSM8K γ=0.85 vs MMLU γ=0.22).\n- **Fisher Information**: I(γ_k) derived, showing AUC≥0.55 structural boundary, AUC≥0.70 practical boundary.\n- **Local independence**: Mitigated by per-benchmark fitting; residual correlations checked (mean r=0.032, max r=0.085).\n- **Inference**: HMC, 4 chains, 2000 warmup + 2000 sampling. R̂<1.01, zero divergences.\n\n### Experiments (Sections 4-5)\n**Setup**: Qwen2.5 (0.5B, 1.5B, 3B) LoRA SFT at 5 dosages (d000-d100), 3 seeds, 3 benchmarks = 45 instances/benchmark. Ground truth from d000.\n\n**Signal Analysis (Section 4)**:\n- Table 1: Signal × Scale AUC at d005. S1 robust (>0.95), S2/S4 fail at 0.5B (~0.47) but recover at 1.5B+ (>0.70).\n- Table 2: Effective signals: 1 at 0.5B, 3 at 1.5B, 4 at 3B.\n- Table 3: Min-K++ directional reversal at d100 (Cohen's d: -1.98 at 0.5B → -1.14 at 3B).\n- Table 4: RRF ablation. RRF 4-signal: 0.962/0.924/0.943. S1-only: 0.979/0.972/0.964. At 0.5B, RRF slightly below S1 (noise dilution). FP robustness: 15% FP → only 2.3% AUC drop.\n\n**Main Results (Section 5)**:\n- Table 5: 8 methods × 5 metrics. ContamCal: 1.8pp MAE [1.2,2.4], 94% coverage, τ=0.96. Best baseline DCR: 3.9pp. Vanilla 4PL: 6.5pp, 58% coverage.\n- Table 6: Per-benchmark MAE. MMLU 1.1, GSM8K 2.8, ARC 1.2.\n- Table 7: γ_k estimates. MMLU 0.22, GSM8K 0.85, ARC 0.18. χ² p=0.002.\n- Table 8: Dose-response 3B GSM8K. d100: 69.7% observed → 16.2% calibrated (true 12.0%, residual 4.2pp).\n- Table 9: Simulation sweep (120 conditions). AUC≥0.70, N≥50 → CI<7pp, coverage≥95%.\n- Table 10: ME model. At σ_e=0.3: ME 93% coverage vs simple 78%. At σ_e=0.5: ME 91% vs simple 65%.\n- Tables 11-12: 7B validation. MAE 1.4pp, coverage 95%, τ=0.97.\n- Table 13: Cross-family (Llama). γ Pearson r=0.91. MAE 2.1pp, coverage 92%.\n- Table 14: Closed-weight 2-signal. At 1.5B+: 2.1-2.8pp MAE, matching DCR.\n- Tables 15-16: Observational (Instruct, DeepSeek-R1, 72B). Wider CIs, GSM8K γ persists.\n\n**Metrics**: MAE, 95%/80%/50% CI coverage, CI width, Kendall τ, dose-response monotonicity.\n\n### Limitations (Section 7)\n6 limitations listed: model family breadth, unidimensional θ, SFT≠real contamination, local independence, closed-weight degradation, computational cost.\n\n## Experiment Design Reference (from review context)\nThe paper covers all 11 planned experiments:\n- exp-002 (signal pipeline) → Table 1\n- exp-003 (RRF ablation) → Table 4\n- exp-004 (simulation sweep) → Table 9\n- exp-005 (noise propagation) → Table 10\n- exp-006 (IRT + baselines) → Table 5\n- exp-007 (7B bridging) → Tables 11-12\n- exp-008 (signal survival multiscale) → Tables 2-3\n- exp-009 (RL observational) → Table 15\n- exp-012 (72B observational) → Table 16\n- exp-013 (closed-weight 2-signal) → Table 14\n- exp-014 (multi-family Llama) → Table 13\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nProvide a detailed review focusing on:\n\n1. **Methodological Soundness**: Is the 4PL+γ IRT formulation well-motivated and correctly specified? Are there identifiability concerns? Is the measurement error model appropriate? Is the Fisher Information derivation correct?\n\n2. **Experimental Rigor**: Are the controlled experiments properly designed? Is the baseline comparison fair? Are the evaluation metrics comprehensive? Are there confounds?\n\n3. **Statistical Validity**: Are confidence intervals properly constructed? Is the simulation study convincing? Are there issues with multiple comparisons?\n\n4. **Weaknesses/Concerns**: What are the main methodological and experimental weaknesses?\n\n5. **Questions for Authors**: Specific technical questions.\n\n## Output Format\n\n```\n## R1 Review: Methods & Experiments\n\n### Summary\n[2-3 sentences]\n\n### Strengths\n[Numbered list, 4-6 items]\n\n### Weaknesses\n[Numbered list, 4-6 items]\n\n### Questions for Authors\n[Numbered list, 3-5 items]\n\n### Minor Issues\n[Numbered list]\n\n### Preliminary Score: X/6\n### Confidence: X/5\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":38260,"cache_read_input_tokens":22964,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":38260},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49fcde5e-0610-4e7e-a894-56110a3c51ee","uuid":"c7442049-1c38-4dec-82d4-189a49192998"}
